From: sluongng <26684313+sluongng@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 11:40:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] jj-core: Bound literal multi-input line comparisons

Stock merge filtering and conflict resolution compare all remove and add
terms simultaneously. Calling the unbounded multi-input diff inside a
request timeout leaves its histogram, LCS and intersection work alive.

Add a separate bounded multi-input API that retains the existing pairwise
literal choices and intersects their matching base ranges. Charge every
pair and intersection before allocation, poll cancellation during traversal,
and retain conservative cumulative allocation accounting across scratch
lifetimes. Keep the existing two-sided API and its quotas unchanged.

This primitive does not materialize conflicts or confer object authority.
Callers still own source admission and must bound merge terms/output.
---
diff --git a/src/diff/bounded.rs b/src/diff/bounded.rs
--- a/src/diff/bounded.rs
+++ b/src/diff/bounded.rs
@@ -14,6 +14,8 @@
 
 use super::*;
 
+mod multi;
+
 /// Limits shared by one or more exact two-sided line comparisons.
 ///
 /// Counts are cumulative, including failed calls. Depth is additionally capped at
diff --git a/src/diff/bounded/multi.rs b/src/diff/bounded/multi.rs
new file mode 100644
--- /dev/null
+++ b/src/diff/bounded/multi.rs
@@ -0,0 +1,127 @@
